{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: trust the published grow release on dap-demo. Head 66c4c77cd37c2f600ee6abb18d183d2b0a8c6c4e, branch planner/demo-trust-row-20261027: one commit on Main aa3ae873, which is the merge base, so it merges cleanly. One path, apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc, with one added line. Review request 6fb581b0, checker promise dbcd9bc6, request 31e35d4e, planner promise 6dea1f53. Artifacts: apps (5814a6f3), apps/room (ae3e1f71) and the file (6ac0f968).\n\nRead order: the diff; then dap-grow's row in apps/room/wrangler.grow.jsonc; the listing reports afa367fa; the coverage decision 2d1bb9a0; the deploy record 7097f15c.\n\nConditions:\n- Configuration only, one path, one line, in the vars block beside APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS.\n- The row equals dap-grow's byte for byte. I parsed both files with the repository's own JSONC reader (configOf in scripts/security-settings.mjs) on an exported tree of the head: the file's name is dap-demo, and its APPLICATION_TRUST string is identical to dap-grow's. It is one row with exactly the keys host, publisher and release: release sha256:71e10ca9…, publisher key_gg4rXwy4…, host github.com. That is the shape readApplicationTrust accepts, and the same row is live on dap-grow, where afa367fa lists it as the one installation.\n- Consistent with docs/deploy.md, which says to add a row only for a release you mean to keep, and with 2d1bb9a0. That decision accepted withdrawal for visitor-room installations on dap-demo and said this one row would follow so the public demo can install the published release.\n- git diff --check is clean, and check-commit-messages reports 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The row admits one exact release from one publisher at one host. No other release becomes trusted. A visitor-room installation of any other release stays refused with application-revoked, as 2d1bb9a0 accepted. The row is not secret, and no secret changes.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. One line, copied exactly.\n\nTwo points for the deploy, not for this head:\n1. With --keep-vars, the deployed APPLICATION_TRUST comes from this file. After the deploy, confirm the live binding equals the file, as 7097f15c did for dap-grow.\n2. This row lets the release be installed and admitted. Its screens are a separate setting: APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS stays [] on dap-demo, so the grow screens are not served there until a host is mapped. If the public demo needs them, that is a separate configuration head.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 66c4c77c. Configuration only; no gate is owed. The planner lands it and deploys dap-demo with --keep-vars.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5814a6f3c72533114d03d115cf4488eea3e21d12","binding":"assigned","head":"66c4c77cd37c2f600ee6abb18d183d2b0a8c6c4e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dbcd9bc6d6793663ece5593ce5fee5693a07a8ce\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6dea1f531260e667e75955ed1d4bd9bd2e82736a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dbcd9bc6d6793663ece5593ce5fee5693a07a8ce","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}